A||||8||KissMySSFiero||For those in the military or that have to be away from their family..||||7||
Z||000000||KissMySSFiero||07-05-2001||04:28 PM||||i was at a Lonestar Concert a few weeks ago.<BR>this is theyre new song.  They had recieve an email from a fan in the military who was in Egypt,  he wanted to request this for his wife who happened to be at the concert that night with hers and his moms.  they brought her on the stage and sang this to her...<P>"He called her on the road<BR>From a lonely cold hotel room<BR>Just to hear her say I love you one more time<BR>When he heard the sound<BR>Of the kids laughing in the backround<BR>Had to wipe away a tear from his eye<P>Little voice came on the phone<BR>Said daddy when ya comin' home<BR>He said the first thing that came to his mind<BR>I'm already there<BR>Take a look around<BR>I'm the sunshine in your hair<BR>I'm the shadow on the ground<BR>I'm the whisper in the wind<BR>I'm your imaginary friend <BR>and I know, I'm in your prayers<BR>Oh I'm already there<P>She got back on that phone<BR>Said I really miss you Darlin'<BR>Don't worry about the kids they'll be all right<BR>Wish I was in your arms<BR>Lyin' right there beside you<BR>but I know I'll be in your dreams tonight<BR>and I'll gently kiss you lips<BR>Touch you with my finger tips<BR>So turn out the light and then close your eyes<P>I'm already there<BR>Don't make a sound<BR>I'm the beat in your heart<BR>I'm the moonlight Shinin' down<BR>I'm the whisper in the wind<BR>and I'll be ther til' the end<BR>and you feel that love that we share<BR>Oh I'm already there<P>We may be a thousand miles a part.<BR>but I'll be with you wherever you are<P>I'm already there<BR>Take a look around<BR>I'm the sunshine in your hair<BR>I'm the shadow on the ground<BR>I'm the whisper in the wind<BR>and I'll be there til the end<BR>and You feel the love that we share<BR>Oh I'm already there....<BR> <BR>I'm already there...."<P><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000001||2xsess||07-05-2001||05:08 PM||||Dude, you just put the biggest lump in my throat with that. I'm in Kosovo right now and the Armed Forces Radio has been playing that song like everyday, and it always makes me think about my wife and family. <P>If you're a country fan that song by Gary Allen (or Owen, not sure yet) titled "Right where I'm supposed to be" is a great one too.<P>Thanks for thinking of us.<P>Jeff<BR>Somewhere in the middle of nowhere in Kosovo!<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 07-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||KissMySSFiero||07-05-2001||06:46 PM||||Gary Allen  "Right Where I Need To Be"<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||07-05-2001||09:30 PM||||Keep you're head down, 2xsess  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>Leaving your family behind does really suck, but as long as they understand why, it makes it a little easier to go.||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||07-06-2001||12:24 AM||||Ditto what 2birds said.(Keep you butt down too, if your like I was it's a bigger target)<BR>Get your job done & come home safe!<BR> from an OLD ex-marine(if there is such a thing)||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierobaby||07-06-2001||01:22 AM||||I love that song it reminds me of my family along time ago when my daddy worked night shift he would be asleep when I got up for school and gone by the time I got home so I never saw him only time I saw him was when he would tuck me into bed Sunday nights. I remeber that so well. it still makes me cry to think about it to this day. It was a really hard time. I was young with little time with my dady but when I had time with him I treasured it. I see him everyday now and actually this Fiero has brought us a little closer. That song also reminds me of my boyfriend I see him once or twice aweek and he calls everyday just to hear my voice and to tell me he loves me I also really like the song holes in the floor of heaven by someone....<BR>heres the lyrics<P><BR>one day shy of 8 years old<BR>and grandma passed away <BR>I was a broken hearted little boy blowin out the birthday cake<BR>how I cried when that sky let go <BR>with a cold and lonesome rain<BR>mama smiled and said "don't be sad child <BR>Grandmas watching you today"<BR>cause theres holes in the floor of heaven<BR>and her tears are pourin down<BR>thats how you knwo shes watching <BR>wishin she could be here now<BR>and sometimes if you're lonely<BR>just remeber she can see<BR>theres holes in the floor of heaven<BR>and shes watchin ove you and me<BR>season come and seasons go<BR>nothing stays the smae<BR>I grew up <BR>fell in love<BR>met a girl who took my name<BR>year by year we made a life in this sleepy little town<BR>I thought we'd grow old together<BR>lord I sure do miss her now<BR>but theres holes in the floor of heaven and her tears are pourin down <BR>thats how I know shes watching <BR>wishin she could be here now<BR>sometimes when I'm lonely<BR>I remeber she can see<BR>theres holes in the floor of heave and shes watchin over you and me<BR>little girl is 23<BR>I walk her down the aisle<BR>its a shame her mom can't be here now<BR>to see her lovely smile<BR>they throw the rice I catch her eye as the rain starts commin down<BR>she takes my hand says daddy don't be said cause I know mamas watchin now<BR>and theres holes in the floor of heaven <BR>and her tears are pourin down <BR>thats how you know shes watchin <BR>wishin she could be here now <BR>and sometimes when I'm lonely <BR>I remeber she can see <BR>yes there holes in the floor of heaven <BR>and shes watchin over you and me<P><BR>isn't that a pretty song!? I love it!! :-) <P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||12
Z||000006||Jaygee79||07-06-2001||09:26 AM||||I love that song. Makes me want to cry every time I hear it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||KissMySSFiero||07-06-2001||11:44 AM||||That song is by Steve Werner(sp)  hes a great songwriter.  Reba McEntire has a song that i love about "the man i never knew"  make me think of my dad.  he always traveled when i was growing up.  i dont know the lyrics but its about the man that she never knew taht lived right down the hall.  but was the one she love the  most.  <P>you all need to listen to more country if you dont already.  to me if  i  can relate to a song it just means that much more.  <P>damn i love music.  =Þ||||reg||1
